WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.367
-One of the key supporters

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.033
of the attempt to overthrow
the 2020 election,

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.334
Congressman Jim Jordan, has said
he'll refuse to cooperate

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.400
with the January 6th
investigation

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.434
just days after fellow pro-coup
Republican Ted Cruz

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.334
went on Fox News
to debase himself

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.300
after calling January 6th
a terrorist attack.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.601
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.267
Well, here we are again
doing a show outside our studio

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.367
due to the world being,

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.167
as Winston Churchill
once called it,

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.834
a giant [bleep]-eating
cluster [bleep]

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.801
He had some bad days.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.834
Today we are in our fifth
remote location

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.100
since the pandemic began,
and not to toot our own horn,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.634
but I think this one
looks the best yet.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:48.067
And not to un-toot
that same horn,

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:50.200
that is a terrible development.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.100
It's not good that we're getting
better at doing our show

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.434
outside the studio because
a virus is running rampant.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.701
If someone told you,
"I'm getting very good

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:59.133
at killing
and cooking my own squirrel,"

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.100
you wouldn't think
that person had hit it big,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.200
although what the [bleep]
do I know?

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.167
Maybe next week, Fox News will
start promoting squirrel meat

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.567
as the new COVID cure-all.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.434
On that note,
when I tested positive,

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.734
I tried to get my hands
on some of that horse paste,

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:14.334
but they were out of it
at my local feed store,

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:17.567
so best I could do was this.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:18.567
Some horse pudding.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:21.701
There's no medicinal value
in it.

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.334
It's not a great snack, either.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.467
You can definitely
taste the horse.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.734
What flavor is it?

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.067
Chocoletariat.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.968
Go ahead, groan.
I can't hear you from home.

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:38.133
Speaking of groaning from home,
I was thankfully symptom-free,

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:41.133
but we did have to self-isolate
with our family all last week.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.467
The first couple of days
were rough,

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.367
but then on day five, I thought,
"You know what?

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:47.834
This time with my children
has been a blessing,"

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:52.534
at which point I realized
the virus had infected my brain.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.567
I do attribute my lack
of symptoms

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:57.267
to the fact that I was
vaccinated and boosted,

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:00.267
because it was definitely not my
natural physical constitution.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.501
I mean, look at me.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:04.567
I have the immune system
of an inbred British king.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:07.400
I once got pneumonia
from looking at a snow globe.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.167
Anyway, we've now done this show
in so many different locations,

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.267
people are starting to think

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.767
I'm in the Witness
Protection Program,

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.400
especially since I took
the stand in that Mafia trial.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.567
I mean, I didn't
actually see anything.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.601
I just thought the trial
would be a good chance

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:20.067
to use my Pacino impression.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.667
[ As Pacino ] I was not
at the scene of the crime

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:26.934
because I was too busy filming
my show in a Zoom Room.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.300
Oh, yeah.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.100
[ Normal voice ] You know,
I thought it would be weird

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.400
doing the Pacino

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.000
without the standing ovation
from the audience,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.300
but it was fine.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.000
It was exactly as rewarding.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.067
Look, I swear -- I swear to God

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.834
I'm going to talk about
the news soon.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.701
But one final piece
of housekeeping.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:47.734
The most popular/most reviled
part of my quarantine shows

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.767
was the talking
sea captain painting.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:52.801
Now, I'm not currently
in my in-laws' home.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:57.167
We have no idea
whose apartment this is.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.767
I'm not currently
in my in-laws' home,

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:02.968
where that painting resides,
but have I got a story for you.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.501
A few months ago, I'm doing
a Q&amp;A with my studio audience,

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.467
and this lovely woman
named Mary LaGarde

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:09.767
said she's an artist
who wants to make me

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.934
my own painting
of the sea captain

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:15.567
in case I do at-home shows
again, to which I said,

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:18.367
"I'm not doing at-home shows
again, you buffoon,"

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:20.167
happily, just in my head,
not out loud,

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.934
because, you know -- you know.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.868
Even better,
Mary said she wanted

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.601
to paint the captain's wife,
too,

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.234
and asked who I thought
the captain's wife

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:29.734
should be based on.

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.501
And, well, I'm not upset
with my choice.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:33.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.167
Ye chose, well, friend.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:41.000
I hereby forgive any ill will
I've had towards ye in the past.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.400
-Oh, man, I'm just so glad
you're happy.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.868
What kind of things
do you do together?

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:48.934
-Well, we both love treasure,
be it rubies, emeralds, or...

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.033
-♪ Diamonds ♪

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.367
-That's great.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.200
Well, I'm on page five

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.634
and I haven't addressed current
events, so you know what?

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.968
I'm going to get back to...

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:59.167
-♪ Work ♪
-That's right.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.667
I'm gonna get back to work.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:04.968
Now, I had a terrible week,
but the one silver lining is,

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:08.200
at no point during the week
was I Ted Cruz.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.133
-Hey, Seth?
-Yeah, bud?

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.868
-Weird question, but, uh,

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:14.234
you know how you text me
my "Closer Look" lines

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.968
and then I record them on my
phone and send them back to you?

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:18.000
-I do, yes.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.434
-Are you also doing that
with Rihanna?

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:22.300
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.767
Because it seems like hers are
maybe just pulled from songs.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.534
-No, no, no.
No, no, no, no.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:30.100
-Okay, sorry I asked.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.167
-Hey, don't you give it
a second thought.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.901
Now, where was I?
Oh, right, Ted Cruz.

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:36.434
Anyways,
as you've probably seen,

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.334
the big news in politics
while I've been away,

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.200
has been the sight
of a United States senator

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.167
going on TV to humiliate himself
and beg for forgiveness

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.901
for the grave sin of condemning
a violent insurrection

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.667
aimed at overthrowing
American democracy.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:50.033
It was so pathetic,
I honestly thought

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.300
I was delirious from the COVID.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.033
But it turns out it was real.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:57.467
And I was just delirious
from my horse pudding.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.534
And look, we all know
Ted Cruz has a thing

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:00.767
for self-humiliation.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.701
He slinked back from Cancún

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.567
after escaping a blackout
in his state.

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:05.934
He endorsed Donald Trump

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:09.367
after Trump insulted his wife
and his father

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.767
and took that infamous photo

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:12.601
where he made campaign calls
for Trump

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:14.767
looking like Jack Lemmon
in "Glengarry Glen Ross."

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:18.367
And he keeps showing up
in public with that facial hair

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:22.200
looking like a Chewbacca who
shaved everything but the beard.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.734
You see, Cruz originally said
what you might think

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:28.000
was a totally
non-controversial thing

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.367
about the anniversary
of the January 6th insurrection.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:34.300
-We are approaching
a solemn anniversary this week,

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.834
and it is an anniversary

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:38.934
of a violent terrorist attack
on the Capitol

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:42.200
where we saw the men
and women of law enforcement

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:46.634
demonstrate incredible courage,
incredible bravery,

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:48.901
risk their lives

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:51.734
to defend the men and women
who serve in this Capitol.

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.267
-I mean, it's the right thing
to say,

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:55.267
even though it's definitely
a little weird

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:57.467
to condemn an attack
you helped whip up

00:05:57.467 --> 00:06:00.067
by spreading the very lies
that fueled that mob.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:01.901
It's like when OJ promised
to find the real killer,

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:03.934
except in Cruz's case,
it's arguably worse

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:06.100
because he's doing it
at the scene of the crime.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.067
Imagine if OJ had gone back to
the house to look for the clues.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:12.300
"Whoa, who left
these gloves here?

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.634
These were supposed to go
in the armoire, guys.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.767
They shrink
if you leave them outside."

00:06:17.767 --> 00:06:20.501
But the actual language Cruz
used was pretty standard fare.

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:23.133
In fact, it's the bare minimum
he should have said.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:25.601
If anything, the only part
that was surprising about it

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:27.300
was that it was
a fairly normal thing

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.200
from a guy
who is anything but normal.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.000
On top of being one of
the most disliked politicians

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.067
on the planet,
he's also one of the weirdest.

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:36.701
Dude posed with a butter cow,
dug into some queso on-camera,

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.200
and appeared to eat
a booger onstage

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.434
during a live national debate
like he was trying to win money

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:42.601
on some weird
Japanese game show.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:45.801
Anyway, the point is, even
that bare-minimum condemnation

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:48.534
of the January 6th attack
was apparently too much

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:51.167
for the new enforcers
of Republican orthodoxy,

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:52.367
like Tucker Carlson.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:53.567
For them, no criticism

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.267
of what happened on January 6th
is allowed,

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:56.801
and their new litmus test

00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:59.133
is that the attempted coup
was a good thing.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.234
So Cruz had to
go on Tucker's show

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:02.467
to grovel and debase himself

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:04.100
and say that
he didn't actually mean

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.367
to condemn
the violent insurrection

00:07:05.367 --> 00:07:06.934
he helped foment on January 6th.

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.300
-You called this
a terror attack,

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.300
when by no definition
was it a terror attack.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.200
That's a lie.
You told that lie on purpose.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.601
And I'm wondering why you did.

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:18.300
-Well, Tucker, thank you
for having me on.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.167
When you aired
your episode last night,

00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:22.667
I sent you a text
shortly thereafter and said,

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:23.934
"Listen, I'd like to go on,"

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:28.033
because the way I phrased things
yesterday, it was sloppy

00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:29.300
and it was, frankly, dumb.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.400
-I don't buy that.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.901
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
I don't buy that.

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:33.200
Look, I've known you
a long time,

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.667
since before you went
to the Senate.

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:37.133
I do not believe that you
used that accidentally.

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:38.300
I just don't.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:41.334
-So, Tucker, as a result
of my sloppy phrasing,

00:07:41.334 --> 00:07:44.033
it's caused a lot of people
to misunderstand what I meant.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:47.367
The reason the phrasing was
sloppy is I have talked dozens,

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:50.234
if not hundreds, of times,
I've drawn a distinction.

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:54.367
I wasn't saying that the
thousands of peaceful protesters

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:57.167
supporting Donald Trump
are somehow terrorists.

00:07:57.167 --> 00:08:01.000
I wasn't saying the millions
of patriots across the country

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.701
supporting President Trump
are terrorists,

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:05.534
and that's what a lot of people
have misunderstood that comment.

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:07.400
-Wait a second.
But even -- Hold on.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.167
What you just said
doesn't make sense.

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.200
-Tucker, I agree with you.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.267
It was a mistake
to say that yesterday.

00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:15.200
-Wow, I knew Ted had a thing
for self-humiliation,

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.567
but that is next level.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:19.300
Imagine begging for forgiveness
from a cable news host

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:22.133
while he sits there with that
look he always has on his face

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:27.467
like he's trying to remember the
name of the other guy from Wham!

00:08:27.467 --> 00:08:30.701
"Was it the talented
Mr. Ripley?"

00:08:30.701 --> 00:08:32.133
That clip was like watching

00:08:32.133 --> 00:08:33.834
one of those dumb
cable news segments

00:08:33.834 --> 00:08:36.100
where a reporter
willingly gets tasered

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.968
just to show everyone
how bad it is.

00:08:37.968 --> 00:08:42.033
-I'm about to receive
50,000 volts of electricity.

00:08:42.033 --> 00:08:43.300
Do it.
[ Taser crackling ]

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.000
[ Groaning ]

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.467
Stop!

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:47.934
Oh!

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:50.968
It hurts.

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:53.901
-Or it was like watching
one of those "Jackass" clips

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:55.834
where someone has to glue
their ass cheeks together

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:57.634
or get smacked by a giant hand.

00:08:57.634 --> 00:08:58.901
-What's up, dude?
-Yeah, dude.

00:08:58.901 --> 00:09:01.200
How about this crowd, brother?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.868
-And those two clips
are from our new segment,

00:09:04.868 --> 00:09:06.434
"Simpler Times."

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:08.734
By the way,
"simpler times" now refers

00:09:08.734 --> 00:09:11.534
to any time before noon today.

00:09:11.534 --> 00:09:13.434
That performance
was so embarrassing,

00:09:13.434 --> 00:09:16.901
Cruz even got mocked
by the graphic under him

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:19.534
as he was talking, which said
"Cruz'ing for a bruising."

00:09:19.534 --> 00:09:21.501
How much more humiliating
can it get?

00:09:21.501 --> 00:09:23.000
That'd be like if my staff

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.634
started putting up graphics
below me

00:09:24.634 --> 00:09:26.567
while I was talking
without my permission,

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:27.968
which could never happen

00:09:27.968 --> 00:09:30.434
because I see every graphic
before it airs on the show.

00:09:30.434 --> 00:09:33.334
I also like how Cruz finds a way
to mention in that clip

00:09:33.334 --> 00:09:35.601
that he texted Tucker
like they're good pals.

00:09:35.601 --> 00:09:37.434
Unfortunately for Ted,
anytime he tries to text

00:09:37.434 --> 00:09:39.534
or call someone,
it comes up as "Spam Likely,"

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:41.834
or, in his case,
"Likely Made of Spam."

00:09:41.834 --> 00:09:43.901
And yet this debacle
keeps getting worse for Cruz

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:47.000
because he proudly tweeted out
the clip of himself groveling,

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.901
which is a little like posting
a video of yourself

00:09:48.901 --> 00:09:50.567
landing nards first
on a handrail

00:09:50.567 --> 00:09:52.467
during a skateboard fail
with the caption,

00:09:52.467 --> 00:09:54.634
"Check out how epic this is."

00:09:54.634 --> 00:09:57.200
But this is the core
of the modern GOP politics.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.601
You have to prove to the base
that you have no dignity,

00:10:00.601 --> 00:10:02.200
that you're willing
to humiliate yourself for them,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.467
and that there's nothing
too pathetic for you to do

00:10:04.467 --> 00:10:05.968
in order to win their favor.

00:10:05.968 --> 00:10:07.367
That's why they all
slinked back to Trump

00:10:07.367 --> 00:10:09.601
after he brutally mocked
and insulted all of them,

00:10:09.601 --> 00:10:11.834
because reverence and loyalty
to Trump above all else

00:10:11.834 --> 00:10:13.567
is the litmus test
for GOP politics.

00:10:13.567 --> 00:10:16.000
That's also why key figures
in the attempted coup

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.234
are now refusing to cooperate
with the investigation

00:10:18.234 --> 00:10:19.467
into what happened on that day,

00:10:19.467 --> 00:10:21.400
like Ohio congressman
Jim Jordan,

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.834
who announced that he won't
cooperate with the committee

00:10:23.834 --> 00:10:26.801
despite repeatedly insisting
he had "nothing to hide,"

00:10:26.801 --> 00:10:29.934
although it certainly seems like
he did have something to hide

00:10:29.934 --> 00:10:32.834
given this incredibly cagey
interview he did a while back

00:10:32.834 --> 00:10:34.367
with a reporter who asked him

00:10:34.367 --> 00:10:37.234
if he talked to President Trump
on the day of the insurrection.

00:10:37.234 --> 00:10:41.367
-Yes or no, did you speak with
President Trump on January 6th?

00:10:41.367 --> 00:10:43.634
-Yeah, I mean, I spoke
with the president last week.

00:10:43.634 --> 00:10:44.734
I speak with the president
all the time.

00:10:44.734 --> 00:10:46.200
I spoke with him on January 6th.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.834
I mean, I talk with
President Trump all the time.

00:10:48.834 --> 00:10:50.834
I'm -- I'm actually
kind of amazed sometimes

00:10:50.834 --> 00:10:52.133
that people keep asking this.

00:10:52.133 --> 00:10:53.467
Of course. I talk with
the president all the time.

00:10:53.467 --> 00:10:55.167
Like I said,
I talked with him last week.

00:10:55.167 --> 00:10:58.033
-On January 6th, did you
speak with him before,

00:10:58.033 --> 00:11:01.767
during, or after
the Capitol was attacked?

00:11:01.767 --> 00:11:04.100
-I'd have to go --
I'd -- I --

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:07.701
I spoke with him that day after,
I think, after.

00:11:07.701 --> 00:11:09.167
I don't know if I spoke with him
in the morning or not.

00:11:09.167 --> 00:11:11.734
I just don't know.
I'd have to go back --

00:11:11.734 --> 00:11:15.033
I mean, I don't --
I don't know that --

00:11:15.033 --> 00:11:17.100
when -- when those
conversations happened.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.234
-[ Stammering ]

00:11:28.667 --> 00:11:31.701
[ Chuckles ] Those were
straightforward questions.

00:11:31.701 --> 00:11:33.968
And he melted down like
a Coen brothers villain.

00:11:33.968 --> 00:11:35.534
If a cop interrogated someone

00:11:35.534 --> 00:11:37.200
and they started talking
like that, they'd open the door

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.534
and shout,
"Yep, yeah, never mind.

00:11:39.534 --> 00:11:42.868
Yeah, we don't -- we don't need
to do good cop/bad cop today.

00:11:42.868 --> 00:11:46.501
This guy's basically --
basically admitted.

00:11:46.501 --> 00:11:48.634
Yeah.
No, I --

00:11:48.634 --> 00:11:51.801
I know you had a whole routine
all set up and ready to go,

00:11:51.801 --> 00:11:55.934
but he's confessed,
so I don't think we --

00:11:55.934 --> 00:11:59.734
I'm sorry, but my partner
has been working on a bad cop.

00:11:59.734 --> 00:12:01.534
It's -- It's Pacino.

00:12:01.534 --> 00:12:04.434
And he'd just really like
to come in here and do it.

00:12:04.434 --> 00:12:05.434
Do you mind?

00:12:05.434 --> 00:12:06.934
Thank you.

00:12:06.934 --> 00:12:08.534
Means the world to him.

00:12:08.534 --> 00:12:11.200
Okay. He agreed.
You can come on in."

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.367
[ As Pacino ]
Whoa, Jim Jordan.

00:12:13.367 --> 00:12:15.501
As I live and breathe.

00:12:15.501 --> 00:12:20.434
We have got you
by the shirt sleeves.

00:12:20.434 --> 00:12:22.734
[ Normal voice ] The point is --
the point --

00:12:22.734 --> 00:12:25.267
there is nothing too humiliating
or pathetic for these guys.

00:12:25.267 --> 00:12:27.901
All that matters to them
is serving Trump

00:12:27.901 --> 00:12:30.133
and the GOP's authoritarian
assault on democracy,

00:12:30.133 --> 00:12:32.334
and they'll embarrass themselves
as much as they have to

00:12:32.334 --> 00:12:33.634
in order to do it.

00:12:33.634 --> 00:12:36.634
And I'm saying that as a guy
who ate horse pudding

00:12:36.634 --> 00:12:38.400
and talks to
a sea captain painting.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.634
I'm now in my fifth
remote location.

00:12:40.634 --> 00:12:43.534
But, hey, at least I'm not back
at my in-laws' house

00:12:43.534 --> 00:12:46.934
or upstairs with the wasps
and the Thorn Birds in my...

00:12:46.934 --> 00:12:48.100
-Attica!

